ISEScan-v2 is a derivative of ISEScan v1.7.3 by Zhiqun Xie and Haixu Tang.
Upstream: https://github.com/xiezhq/ISEScan
Revision: 83a74eccb0eef89674e1e49fba31cb4cab29018f
ISEScan source and the two supplied transposase reference files are distributed
in that upstream release under its Apache-2.0 repository license. The files have
no separate license notice. No independent ISfinder database is included.
Cite: Xie and Tang, Bioinformatics 33(21), 3340–3347 (2017),
https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btx433 .

SSW components retain the MIT notices in ssw201507/license.ssw.txt and source
headers (Boston College; Clement and Adrien Leger wrapper). kseq.h retains
its MIT notice, copyright Genome Research Ltd. License texts are preserved.

Modified for CRISPRloci on 2026-10-12: source-relative reference/library lookup;
shell-free native command vectors; native BLAST error propagation; bounded
FASTA/TSV validation, process containment and source-bound JSON output. The
scientific thresholds and reference models are unchanged.

Modified on 2026-10-13: shared HMM completion checks; indexed ranked ORF lookup
and interval overlap discovery; rejected inconsistent BLAST query/source/self
binding and double-gap TIR columns; ensured temporary subject and export handle
cleanup; removed unused archived export work. Native distances, thresholds,
classification, command arguments and model identities remain unchanged.

Native runtime dependencies are separate programs, not included in this source
repository. Preserve their package licenses in deployed/distributed runtimes:
FragGeneScan 1.32 (GNU GPL, version unspecified in the exact source README;
the Bioconda BSD metadata conflicts with the authoritative source notice); HMMER 3.4 (BSD-3-Clause); NCBI BLAST+ (public-domain
NCBI component plus third-party notices). Python libraries retain their own
licenses: NumPy/SciPy (BSD), Biopython (Biopython/BSD), fastcluster (BSD).
